---
import LandingPage from "../layouts/LandingPage.astro";
import { APP_URL } from "../lib/config";
import { SITE_URL, articleJsonLd, faqJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";

const UPDATED = "2026-08-25";
const canonical = "/features";
const title = "Features — Focus rooms, synced timers, quiet accountability";
const description =
  "Everything Refocus does: 25/50/75 minute sessions, focus mode, synced timers, friends, and community — free to start, no credit card.";

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What does Refocus include?",
    answer:
      "Timed focus sessions (25, 50, or 75 minutes), partner matching, synced timers, quiet mics with cameras on for presence, friends and session requests, and a community layer between sessions.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need my camera on?",
    answer:
      "Cameras stay on so your partner can see you're there. Focus mode mutes mics by default — you're present, not performing. Unmute at the end if you want a short check-in, and you can turn your camera off anytime.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is it free?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Refocus is free to start with no credit card. See the pricing page for what's included.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is this a group lobby or a one-to-one room?",
    answer:
      "One-to-one. You work with a single partner and a shared timer — not a crowded Discord or Zoom lobby. That keeps the session quiet and accountable.",
  },
];

const article = articleJsonLd({
  headline: "Refocus features",
  description,
  path: canonical,
  dateModified: UPDATED,
});

const softwareJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
  name: "Refocus",
  url: SITE_URL,
  applicationCategory: "ProductivityApplication",
  operatingSystem: "Web",
  description,
  offers: {
    "@type": "Offer",
    price: "0",
    priceCurrency: "USD",
  },
  installUrl: `${APP_URL}/auth/sign-up`,
  featureList: [
    "25, 50, and 75 minute focus sessions",
    "Accountability partner matching",
    "Synced timers",
    "Quiet focus mode",
    "Friends and session requests",
    "Community between sessions",
  ],
};
---

<LandingPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  eyebrow="Product"
  heading="Everything Refocus does, in one page."
  lead="Nothing you don't need. A timer, a partner, a room. The rest stays out of the way — free to start, no credit card."
  updated={UPDATED}
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaTitle="Try it in a real session"
  ctaText="Pick a length, get matched with someone who's also there to focus, and work side by side with a shared timer."
  ctaHref={`${APP_URL}/auth/sign-up`}
  ctaLabel="Start a free session"
  jsonLd={[article, softwareJsonLd, faqJsonLd(faqs)]}
>
  <h2>The session flow</h2>
  <p>
    Refocus is a ritual, not a dashboard tour. Every feature exists to support
    one loop: match → share a goal → work with a synced timer → check in when
    time is up.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Match</strong> — get paired with someone else who is ready to
      focus, or invite a friend you already know.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Goal</strong> — say what you are working on in one line so both of
      you start with intent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Focus</strong> — mics stay quiet; cameras stay on for presence;
      the timer runs for both of you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Checkout</strong> — when the block ends, optionally unmute for a
      short check-in, then leave with the work done (or clearer).
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    That is the same idea as
    <a href="/body-doubling">body doubling</a> and a quiet
    <a href="/focus-room">online focus room</a> — co-presence without a meeting.
  </p>

  <h2>Three lengths. One ritual.</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>25-minute</strong> sprints for quick wins, <strong>50-minute</strong>
    deep-work blocks for the real thing, and <strong>75-minute</strong>
    marathons for writing or research. Pick a length, start the timer — the
    structure does the rest. Students often stack two 50s for exam prep; remote
    workers often protect a single 75 for deep work.
  </p>

  <h2>Focus mode</h2>
  <p>
    Both mics muted by default. Cameras stay on for presence. You're present,
    not performing. Unmute at the end of the session to check in if you want.
    That's the same idea as a library desk — co-presence without a meeting.
  </p>
  <p>
    If “just focus” advice has never worked for ADHD-like brains, quiet presence
    is often the missing piece. Start with a short block and our
    <a href="/body-doubling">body doubling</a> guide.
  </p>

  <h2>Synced timers</h2>
  <p>
    When your partner starts, you start. Breaks land together. No coordination
    overhead — sit down and the timer takes care of the rhythm. See also our
    guides on <a href="/focus-room">online focus rooms</a> and
    <a href="/virtual-coworking">virtual coworking</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Friends and session requests</h2>
  <p>
    Work with the people you focus best with. Send friend requests, send session
    requests, and see who's free, who's in a session, and how long is left on
    their timer. Random matching is fine for a first session; friends make the
    habit stick.
  </p>

  <h2>Community between sessions</h2>
  <p>
    Share wins, ask for advice, and cheer others on when you're not in a room —
    quiet company while you work, supportive community when you don't. The room
    stays one-to-one; the lounge is optional.
  </p>

  <h2>Built for different kinds of deep work</h2>
  <h3>Students &amp; exams</h3>
  <p>
    Timed blocks for JEE, NEET, UPSC, CA, and other long prep seasons —
    especially when studying alone at home feels endless. Pair with
    <a href="/study-with-me">study with me</a> and
    <a href="/study-partner">study partner</a> if that is your main use case.
  </p>
  <h3>Remote workers &amp; freelancers</h3>
  <p>
    A container for deep work when Slack and Zoom eat the day. Refocus is not
    another meeting — it is a scheduled quiet block with a partner. Compare
    approaches on our
    <a href="/focusmate-alternative">Focusmate alternative</a> page.
  </p>
  <h3>ADHD-friendly accountability</h3>
  <p>
    Task initiation is often harder than the work itself. Having someone else
    “there” lowers the activation energy without forcing conversation. Read
    <a href="/body-doubling">body doubling</a>, then try a 25-minute session.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Free to start with no credit card. See what's included on the
    <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.
  </p>
</LandingPage>
